  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 222 AM MDT Sun May 31 2026\n\nLow pressure system that brought impressive rains to parts of \neast Idaho will move north into Montana today. Many locations \nacross the upper Snake Plain and into the upper Snake highlands \nhave seen an inch or more of rainfall. Additional rainfall today\nwill be limited north of a line from Arco to Idaho Falls to \nPalisades and north. These areas could see up to an additional \n0.10 inches today. Temperatures will still run a touch on the \ncool side today with highs ranging from the 60s for the \nmountains, highlands and upper Snake Plain to lower 70s for the \nlower Snake Plain and Magic Valley. Tonight should be the \ncoldest night with overnight lows falling into the 30s even into\nthe Snake River Plain. However temps probably staying just warm\nenough that a widespread frost is unlikely. With that said, \nthere could be some colder pockets that fall to near or slightly\nbelow freezing. \n\nTemperatures rebound fully by Tuesday with temps ranging from the \n70s to low 80s. Models continue to pick up on a weak trough passing \nthrough Wednesday Night into Thursday. However it looks like most of \nthe moisture with this system will stay north of the area with only \nlow chances for precipitation for east Idaho. Otherwise, warm dry \nweather should prevail for the middle and latter part of the week.",
